From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:20:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: a switch that keeps the domains of the groups as they
 are

The file "type" of each group of the IOMMU in sysfs changes the default
domain of the group: whoever is root unbinds the drivers of a group,
writes "identity", and binds them again. A system that starts with DMA
translation (iommu.passthrough=0) so that a device whose firmware root
has replaced cannot reach the memory of the kernel and undo a lockdown
loses that protection to one write. The lockdown does not look at it.

kernel.iommu_group_type_locked closes that. Once it is set, a write to
the file of any group is refused, and the kernel log says so. It can be
set and not cleared, as kernel.modules_disabled. What each group has
stays as it is.

For the entries of LibreELEC Hades that start with DMA translation and
the kernel locked down: their init sets it once it has mounted the boot
partition, which may have needed the USB controllers taken out of the
translation for that start (a laptop whose firmware leaves part of what
they reach out of its tables of the IOMMU).
---
 drivers/iommu/iommu.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
index b486b8b..0a54a98 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include <trace/events/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/sched/mm.h>
 #include <linux/msi.h>
+#include <linux/sysctl.h>
 #include <uapi/linux/iommufd.h>
 #include <linux/generic_pt/iommu.h>
 
@@ -2949,6 +2950,34 @@ int report_iommu_fault(struct iommu_domain *domain, struct device *dev,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(report_iommu_fault);
 
+/*
+ * kernel.iommu_group_type_locked: once it is set, the default domain of a
+ * group of the IOMMU is no longer changed from user space (the file "type" of
+ * each group in sysfs). Without it, whoever is root takes a device out of DMA
+ * translation: unbind its driver, write "identity" to its group, bind the
+ * driver again; and a device whose firmware root has replaced (the kernel
+ * loads firmware from files) then reaches all memory, the kernel's too, which
+ * undoes a lockdown.
+ *
+ * It can be set and not cleared, like kernel.modules_disabled. It is for a
+ * system that starts with DMA translation and the kernel locked down, and sets
+ * it once what it needs before user space runs is done.
+ */
+static int iommu_group_type_locked;
+
+static const struct ctl_table iommu_group_type_sysctl_table[] = {
+	{
+		.procname	= "iommu_group_type_locked",
+		.data		= &iommu_group_type_locked,
+		.maxlen		= sizeof(int),
+		.mode		= 0644,
+		/* only a transition from "0" to "1" */
+		.proc_handler	= proc_dointvec_minmax,
+		.extra1		= SYSCTL_ONE,
+		.extra2		= SYSCTL_ONE,
+	},
+};
+
 static int __init iommu_init(void)
 {
 	iommu_group_kset = kset_create_and_add("iommu_groups",
@@ -2956,6 +2985,7 @@ static int __init iommu_init(void)
 	BUG_ON(!iommu_group_kset);
 
 	iommu_debugfs_setup();
+	register_sysctl_init("kernel", iommu_group_type_sysctl_table);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -3262,6 +3292,13 @@ static ssize_t iommu_group_store_type(struct iommu_group *group,
 	if (WARN_ON(!group) || !group->default_domain)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* see kernel.iommu_group_type_locked above iommu_init() */
+	if (READ_ONCE(iommu_group_type_locked)) {
+		pr_notice_ratelimited("the domain of group %d is not changed: kernel.iommu_group_type_locked is set\n",
+				      group->id);
+		return -EPERM;
+	}
+
 	if (sysfs_streq(buf, "identity"))
 		req_type = IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDENTITY;
 	else if (sysfs_streq(buf, "DMA"))
